    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nThis beautifully presented one bedroom, first floor apartment is ideally located in the heart of Dublin's city centre on what is one of the capital's finest Georgian streets. Linking Parnell Street to Great Denmark Street and only a few minutes' walk to O'Connell Street, North Great George's Street is a great location and ideal for those who appreciate the splendour of this historic part of the city.\n\nThe apartment is located to the rear of the development with great views of the city and benefitting from a designated car parking space, a rarity in the city centre.\n\nThe accommodation comprises a hallway with storage closet and separate hot-press. The living room/ dining room is a large space and full of light with door to a small balcony, wooden flooring and a pretty marble fireplace as a focal point. Off this room, the kitchen is fitted with a range of floor and wall units. The bedroom is a generous sized double with fitted wardrobes, and a bathroom completes the accommodation. There is the benefit of an attic storage space accessed from the hallway.\n\nNorth Great George's Street is only a short stroll to a host of amenities, including city centre shopping, theatres, restaurants and cafés. The abundance of transport links on your doorstep, including a short stroll to both the Green and Red LUAS lines and mainline rail services, makes access across the city and further afield extremely convenient. Combined with the numerous bus routes available nearby, this also provides easy access to Dublin's main universities and colleges."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hallway - 3m x 1m\nWith wooden floor, storage closet which offers valuable storage space and separate hot press.\n\nLiving Room/ Dining Room - 5.6m x 4.4m\nThis is a large bright space with wooden floor and a pretty marble fireplace as a focal point, A window allows plenty of light into the room and a door gives access to a small balcony. The room has ample room for a seating area and dining area.\n\nKitchen - 2.5m x 1.7m\nFitted with a range of floor and wall units with integrated oven, hob and extractor and plumbing for a washing machine. Tiled floor and splashback.\n\nBedroom - 3.4m x 3.3m\nThe bedroom is a generous sized double with a great range of fitted wardrobes.\n\nBathroom - 2.2m x 2.1m\nComprising w.c, wash hand basin and bath with Triton shower attachment.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Spacious first floor apartment</li><li>Located on one of Dublin's best preserved Georgian streets</li><li>Stylish modern decoration</li><li>Designated car parking space</li><li>Attic storage</li><li>Secure bicycle shed at the rear of the building</li><li>Only a few minutes' walk to O'Connell Street</ul>"
      },
